    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule in the owner-creation flow.\n\n**Change:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` handler (`addOwner`) now rejects creation with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners. I added:\n\n- A `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant and a `cityOwnerCount(Owner)` helper that counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitively, consistent with the existing `nextCustomerCode` city comparison).\n- A guard early in `addOwner` \u2014 after address normalization and before the save \u2014 returning `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` when `cityOwnerCount(owner) >= CITY_CAPACITY`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a unique city to exactly 50, expects the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full test suite builds green.",
